        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): nest Settings pages under /settings routes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nControl UI Settings pages currently live at several top-level URLs, so Settings navigation does not have a single canonical URL namespace. This proposes `/settings/*` as the canonical Settings route family while preserving existing top-level deep links.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSettings route metadata now points navigation and programmatic route generation at `/settings/general`, `/settings/appearance`, and the rest of the `/settings/*` pages. Existing top-level paths such as `/config`, `/appearance`, `/channels`, `/debug`, and `/logs` remain registered as aliases so old links still resolve to the same route ids.\n\nThis intentionally does not change Settings layout, sidebar structure, visual styling, form placement, or content organization.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get canonical Settings URLs under `/settings/*`; existing bookmarks and direct links to the older top-level Settings paths continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated locally:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/app-navigation.test.ts ui/src/app-navigation-groups.test.ts`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 ui/src/app-route-paths.ts ui/src/pages/config/route.ts ui/src/pages/channels/route.ts ui/src/pages/debug/route.ts ui/src/pages/logs/route.ts ui/src/app-navigation.test.ts ui/src/app-navigation-groups.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n- Route resolver smoke: `/settings/general -> config`, `/settings/appearance -> appearance`, `/appearance -> appearance`\n\nSkipped by request: local `codex /review` and autoreview.\n",
